        notes: 'Verified against TWOIAF, The Targaryen Kings section. AGOT Appendix lists ''259-262 Jaehaerys II second son of Aegon the Unlikely''. Source text: THE TRAGEDY OF Summerhall brought Jaehaerys, the Second of His Name, to the Iron Throne in 259 AC... The new king was four-and-thirty years of age as he ascended the Iron Throne. No one would have called him formidable.'
